NODE id=matrix/construct/transport.ApplyPatch kind=func
  digest=b3:44d978a46db80ecb6c105a6465479934f7e3cc81ab42d934129494fffc69a47f file=construct/transport/patch.go range=14:70 lang=go exported=true byte_range=290:2342
  sig=func ApplyPatch(base, patch *schema.Surface) (*schema.Surface, error)
  doc=ApplyPatch folds a construct.surface.patch increment onto an existing\nsurface, returning a NEW surface (the base is never mutated). It is the\ncanonical progressive-merge definition; the client renderer mirrors it so\nthe live tap and replay converge to the same state. Semantics by kind:\n\n  - Stream:   APPEND the patch chunks (dedup by chunk seq -> idempotent on\n    replay); Closed latches true; non-empty Source/Title overwrite.\n  - Timeline: UPSERT the patch steps by step id (status/detail/ref update,\n    new ids append); non-empty Title overwrites.\n  - all other kinds: REPLACE the payload wholesale (full re-render). This is\n    how an answered Ask attaches its Response, or a Metric updates its value.\n\nEnvelope decoration carried on the patch (ref/seq/parent/attributes) is\napplied when present. The patch must match the base kind.
EDGES
  calls=matrix/construct/transport.clone,matrix/construct/transport.mergeStream,matrix/construct/transport.mergeTimeline
  references=matrix/construct/schema.KindStream,matrix/construct/schema.KindTimeline,matrix/construct/schema.Surface,matrix/construct/transport.base,matrix/construct/transport.clone,matrix/construct/transport.err,matrix/construct/transport.mergeStream,matrix/construct/transport.mergeTimeline,matrix/construct/transport.out,matrix/construct/transport.patch
  ^defines=matrix/construct/transport/patch.go

